# SvelteKit 2 Forms and Actions

Cursor: SvelteKit 2 form actions live in `+page.server.ts`. Progressive enhancement uses the `use:enhance` directive from `$app/forms`. The canonical type-safe stack is `sveltekit-superforms` + `formsnap` + `zod`. Target: `@sveltejs/kit ^2.60.1`, `sveltekit-superforms ^2.30.1`, `formsnap ^2.0.1`, `zod ^4.4.3`.

The companion `sveltekit-anti-patterns` rule rejects the SvelteKit 1 shapes (entries #19, #24, #25, #32).

## Plain form actions

Default action:

```ts
// src/routes/login/+page.server.ts
import { fail, redirect } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import type { Actions, PageServerLoad } from './$types'

export const load: PageServerLoad = async ({ locals }) => {
  if (locals.user) redirect(303, '/dashboard')
  return {}
}

export const actions: Actions = {
  default: async ({ request, cookies, locals }) => {
    const data = await request.formData()
    const email = String(data.get('email') ?? '')
    const password = String(data.get('password') ?? '')

    if (!email || !password) {
      return fail(400, { email, missing: true })
    }

    const session = await locals.auth.signIn(email, password)
    if (!session) return fail(401, { email, invalid: true })

    cookies.set('session', session.id, {
      path: '/',
      httpOnly: true,
      secure: true,
      sameSite: 'lax',
      maxAge: 60 * 60 * 24 * 7,
    })
    redirect(303, '/dashboard')
  },
}
```

Named actions:

```ts
export const actions: Actions = {
  login: async (event) => { /* ... */ },
  logout: async ({ cookies }) => {
    cookies.delete('session', { path: '/' })
    redirect(303, '/login')
  },
}
```

```svelte
<form method="POST" action="?/login">...</form>
<form method="POST" action="?/logout">...</form>
```

## `use:enhance` for progressive enhancement

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { enhance } from '$app/forms'
  import type { ActionData } from './$types'

  let { form }: { form: ActionData } = $props()
  let submitting = $state(false)
</script>

<form
  method="POST"
  use:enhance={({ formElement, formData, action, cancel }) => {
    submitting = true
    return async ({ result, update }) => {
      submitting = false
      await update()
    }
  }}
>
  <input name="email" type="email" value={form?.email ?? ''} required />
  <input name="password" type="password" required />
  {#if form?.invalid}<p class="error">Invalid credentials.</p>{/if}
  <button disabled={submitting}>Sign in</button>
</form>
```

The v2 callback args are `formElement` and `formData`, NOT the v1 `form` / `data`.

## File uploads require `enctype="multipart/form-data"`

SvelteKit 2 throws under `use:enhance` if a form contains `<input type="file">` without the multipart enctype.

```svelte
<form
  method="POST"
  enctype="multipart/form-data"
  use:enhance
>
  <input type="file" name="avatar" accept="image/*" />
  <button>Upload</button>
</form>
```

## `sveltekit-superforms` + `formsnap` + `zod`

The documented Svelte 5 forms stack. One Zod schema; superforms wires the server validation, the client validation, the error mapping, the constraints, and the typed return value. Source: https://superforms.rocks

Schema:

```ts
// src/routes/login/schema.ts
import { z } from 'zod'

export const loginSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  password: z.string().min(8),
})
export type LoginSchema = typeof loginSchema
```

Server load + action:

```ts
// src/routes/login/+page.server.ts
import { fail, redirect } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import { superValidate } from 'sveltekit-superforms'
import { zod } from 'sveltekit-superforms/adapters'
import type { PageServerLoad, Actions } from './$types'
import { loginSchema } from './schema'

export const load: PageServerLoad = async () => ({
  form: await superValidate(zod(loginSchema)),
})

export const actions: Actions = {
  default: async ({ request, cookies, locals }) => {
    const form = await superValidate(request, zod(loginSchema))
    if (!form.valid) return fail(400, { form })

    const session = await locals.auth.signIn(form.data.email, form.data.password)
    if (!session) {
      return fail(401, { form, message: 'Invalid credentials' })
    }

    cookies.set('session', session.id, { path: '/', httpOnly: true })
    redirect(303, '/dashboard')
  },
}
```

Client form with `formsnap`:

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/login/+page.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  import { superForm } from 'sveltekit-superforms'
  import { zodClient } from 'sveltekit-superforms/adapters'
  import { Field, Control, Label, FieldErrors } from 'formsnap'
  import { loginSchema } from './schema'
  import type { PageData } from './$types'

  let { data }: { data: PageData } = $props()

  const sf = superForm(data.form, {
    validators: zodClient(loginSchema),
  })
  const { form, errors, enhance, submitting } = sf
</script>

<form method="POST" use:enhance>
  <Field form={sf} name="email">
    <Control>
      {#snippet children({ props })}
        <Label>Email</Label>
        <input {...props} type="email" bind:value={$form.email} />
      {/snippet}
    </Control>
    <FieldErrors />
  </Field>

  <Field form={sf} name="password">
    <Control>
      {#snippet children({ props })}
        <Label>Password</Label>
        <input {...props} type="password" bind:value={$form.password} />
      {/snippet}
    </Control>
    <FieldErrors />
  </Field>

  <button disabled={$submitting}>Sign in</button>
</form>
```

## `fail()` re-renders the form with the bad data

```ts
return fail(400, { form, email, missing: true })
```

The `form` prop in `+page.svelte` receives the value. Use it to repopulate inputs and show inline errors.

## Why these matter for LLM output

Pre-2024 trained models will produce:

- `cookies.set` without `path` (anti-pattern #19)
- `use:enhance={({ form, data }) => ...}` instead of `formElement` / `formData` (anti-pattern #24)
- File-upload forms without `enctype="multipart/form-data"` (anti-pattern #25)
- Felte (`createForm` / `@felte/validator-zod`) instead of `sveltekit-superforms` (anti-pattern #32)
